WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.677
This is a child’s upper jaw at about 10. Baby teeth are blue and adult teeth are yellow.

00:00:06.477 --> 00:00:11.960
The adult canine is high in the bone. It moves down on the cheek side and takes the baby canine’s place.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.899
Sometimes it grows towards the palate instead, and the baby canine stays.

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:19.737
It often cannot come through by itself,

00:00:19.737 --> 00:00:22.349
and it can wear away the roots of the front teeth.

00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:27.437
Taking out the baby canine at about 10 to 13 years can help it come through.
